return {
["02:00"]={"“The clock in the centre on the wall in the cafe chimed to announce it was \003Two o’clock in the morning\004. In the middle of the night, everything was silent.”","Before the Coffee Gets Cold: Tales from the Cafe","Toshikazu Kawaguchi"},
["02:01"]={"I checked my watch. \0032:01 am.\004 The cheeseburger Happy Meal was now only a distant memory. I cursed myself for not also ordering a breakfast sandwich for the morning.","The Selected Works of T.S. Spivet","Reif Larsen"},
["02:02"]={"“The middle of the night?” Alec asked sharply. “Can you be more definite?”\n“\003About two. Just past.\004” Daisy noted that he expressed no concern for her safety.","Dead in the Water","Carola Dunn"},
["02:03"]={"Wake up.\n“Having the worst dream.”\n“I should certainly say you were.”\n“It was awful. It just went on and on.”\n“I shook you and shook you and.”\n“Time is it.”\n“It’s nearly — \003almost 2:04\004.”","Oblivion","David Foster Wallace"},
["02:04"]={"Wake up.\n“Having the worst dream.”\n“I should certainly say you were.”\n“It was awful. It just went on and on.”\n“I shook you and shook you and.”\n“Time is it.”\n“It’s nearly — almost \0032:04\004.”","Oblivion","David Foster Wallace"},
["02:05"]={"\0032:05 A.M.\004, Flushing, Queens\nHer cellphone, set on vibrate, rested on the night table next to the bed.","Warrior Monk","Ray Keating"},
["02:06"]={"The middle of the night? Alec asked sharply. “Can you be more definite?”\n“\003About two. Just past.\004” Daisy noted that he expressed no concern for her safety.","Dead in the Water","Carola Dunn"},
["02:07"]={"But I couldn’t sleep. And I got out of bed at \0032:07 a.m.\004 and I felt scared of Mr. Shears so I went downstairs and out of the front door into Chapter Road.","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["02:08"]={"She dressed quickly, and finished tying the second sneaker. The clock now said \0032:08\004.","Warrior Monk","Ray Keating"},
["02:09"]={"\0032:09 AM\004, Jamaica, Queens\nOutside the al-Dawla home, FBI agents were in position — not only on the ground, but also on the partial first story roof outside the second floor bedroom windows.","Warrior Monk","Ray Keating"},
["02:10"]={"“\003Ten minutes past two\004, sir,” answered the man, looking at the clock and blinking. “Ten minutes past two? How horribly late!”","The Picture of Dorian Gray","Oscar Wilde"},
["02:11"]={"Well hidden, each phone waited like an amoral soldier, devoid of compassion, for its orders. And those orders came at precisely \0032:11\004:17 AM EST.","Warrior Monk","Ray Keating"},
["02:12"]={"At \003two twelve A.M.\004, Werner knows, the Frenchman will broadcast again, and Werner will have to switch off the transceiver or else pretend that he hears only static.","All the Light We Cannot See","Anthony Doerr"},
["02:13"]={"Now, listen: your destination is Friday, 4 August 1944, and the window will punch through at 22:30 hours. You’re going to a dimension that diverged from our own at \00302:13\004 on the morning of Wednesday 20 February 1918, over twenty-six years earlier. You don’t know what it’s going to be like.","The Second Internet Cafe, Part 1: The Dimension Researcher","Chris James"},
["02:14"]={"There are no more lights on now than when he arrived. That’s something to be positive about. No great commotion in the building after the shooting. A glance at the clock in the car: \003fourteen minutes past two\004.","How a Gunman Says Goodbye","Malcolm Mackay"},
["02:15"]={"At \0032:15 am\004 a policeman observed the place in darkness, but with the stranger’s motor still at the curb.","The Shadow Out of Time","H.P. Lovecraft"},
["02:16"]={"Didn’t you hear what I told you in the aircraft? General Scott’s aircraft crashed in the desert at \00302:16 hours\004 this morning, killing all aboard.","Echo of Tomorrow","Rob Buckman"},
["02:17"]={"One of the “choppers” stopped, did an about-turn and came back to me. The flare spluttered and faded, and now the glare of the spotlight blinded me. I sat very still. It was \0032:17\004. Against the noise of the blades a deeper resonant sound bit into the chill black air.","The Ipcress File","Len Deighton"},
["02:18"]={"It was \0032:18 in the morning\004, and Donna could see no one else in any other office working so late.","Moo","Jane Smiley"},
["02:19"]={"With the secondary reduction gear useless, there was no way the Petros Jupiter could proceed and at \00302:19\004 the master contacted Land’s End coastguard station on VHF to inform the watch officer of the situation and enquire about the availability of a tug.","The Black Tide","Hammond Innes"},
["02:20"]={"She turned abruptly to the nurse and asked the time. ‘\003Two-twenty\004’ ‘Ah… Two-twenty!’ Genevieve repeated, as though there was something urgent to be done.","Southern Mail","Antoine de Saint Exupery"},
["02:21"]={"\0032:21 a.m.\004 Lance-Corporal Hartmann emerged from the house in the Rue de Londres.","The Night of the Generals","Hans Hellmut Kirst"},
["02:22"]={"Abruptly her stomach growled. She had been too keyed up to eat very much after the accident, and now hunger pangs her in in earnest.\nShe glanced at the clock again.\n\0032:22 A.M.\004","Code Name: Princess","Christina Skye"},
["02:24"]={"It was \0032:24 am\004. She stumbled out of bed, tripping on her shoes that she’d kicked off earlier and pulled on a jumper.","After You’d Gone","Maggie O’Farrell"},
["02:25"]={"It’s \0032:25 in the morning\004, and Sean is calling. Stephen quietly slipped out of bed, and exited the bedroom. With Sean, it could be a family matter, a threat to the country, or countless things in between.","The Traitor","Ray Keating"},
["02:26"]={"Listened to a voicemail message left at \0032:26 am\004 by Claude.","The Lighted Rooms","Richard Mason"},
["02:27"]={"The hands of all the four thousand electric clocks in all the Bloomsbury Centre’s four thousand rooms marked \003twenty-seven minutes past two\004.","Brave New World","Aldous Leonard Huxley"},
["02:28"]={"\0032:28 am\004: Ran out of sheep and began counting other farmyard animals.","Mr. Commitment","Mike Gayle"},
["02:29"]={"He didn’t have to deal with notoriously bad Italian drivers at \003nearly 2:30 in the morning\004, and the safehouse was just a few streets away from the Colosseum, a structure that had been standing in Rome since opening in 80 A.D.","Vatican Shadows","Ray Keating"},
["02:30"]={"It is \0032:30 am\004 and I am tight. As a tick, as a lord, as a newt. Must write this down before the sublime memories fade and blur.","Any Human Heart","William Boyd"},
["02:31"]={"And then I woke up because there were people shouting in the flat and it was \0032:31 a.m.\004 And one of the people was Father and I was frightened.","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["02:32"]={"The last guests departed at \0032:32 a.m.\004, two hours and two minutes after the scheduled completion time.","The Rosie Project","Graeme Simsion"},
["02:33"]={"But it wasn’t going on! It was two-thirty-four, well. \003Two-thirty-three\004 and nothing had happened. Suppose he got a room call, or the elevator night-bell rang, now.","A Swell-looking Babe","Jim Thompson"},
["02:34"]={"But it wasn’t going on! It was \003two-thirty-four\004, well. Two-thirty-three and nothing had happened. Suppose he got a room call, or the elevator night-bell rang, now.","A Swell-looking Babe","Jim Thompson"},
["02:35"]={"Rorschach’s journal: Left Jacob’s house \0032:35 a.m.\004 He knows nothing about any attempt to discredit Dr. Manhattan. He has simply been used.","Watchmen","Alan Moore and Dave Gibbons"},
["02:36"]={"It was about \0032:36 am\004 when a provost colonel arrived to arrest me. At 2:36 1/2 I remembered the big insulating gauntlets. But even had I remembered before, what could I have done?","The Ipcress File","Len Deighton"},
["02:37"]={"June 13, 1990. \003Thirty-seven minutes past two\004 in the morning. And sixteen seconds.","The Stand","Stephen King"},
["02:39"]={"Noo, there’s a report come in fra’ the station-master at Pinwherry that there was a gentleman tuk the \0032:39\004 at Pinwherry.","Five Red Herrings","Dorothy L. Sayers"},
["02:40"]={"When her watch showed \003two-forty\004, she was ready to leave. She put on her darkest coat, a large box of matches already in her pocket, and tied a scarf over her head.","The Private Patient","P.D. James"},
["02:41"]={"His aides had wanted a long, flowery announcement filled with stirring phrases and fulsome praise for their various generals. Eisenhower had tossed their suggestions aside and written — ah! there it is: “The mission of this Allied force was fulfilled at \00302:41\004 local time, May 7, 1945.”","Moonwar","Ben Bova"},
["02:42"]={"This time it was a bird, a crow, wearing the goggles. Patterson had decrypted the telegram, and now read it quickly. GODDESS 4 reports that GENIUS left the salon at \00302:42\004 ZULU.","Night Heron","Adam Brookes"},
["02:43"]={"She settled back beside him. “It’s \0032:43\004:12 am, Case. Got a readout chipped into my optic nerve.”","Neuromancer","William Gibson"},
["02:44"]={"You got here at \003sixteen minutes to three\004. Ron looked at his watch.","The Abominable Man","Maj Sjöwall"},
["02:45"]={"\0030245h\004., Ennet House, the hours that are truly wee.","Infinite Jest","David Foster Wallace"},
["02:46"]={"Vicki shoved her glasses at her face and peered at the clock. \003Two forty-six\004. ‘I don’t have time for this’ she muttered, settling back against the pillows, heart still slamming against her ribs.","Blood Lines","Tanya Huff"},
["02:47"]={"The glowing numbers read \0032:47 am\004. Moisés sighs and turns back to the bathroom door. Finally, the doorknob turns and Conchita comes back to bed. She resumes her place next to Moisés. Relieved, he pulls her close.","The Book of Want","Daniel A. Olivas"},
["02:48"]={"And you keep quiet, Betty. There may be trouble. He almost pushed her off the desk toward Max. A second later he had darkened the room by flicking the switch by the foyer door. Through the door, the clock showed \003twelve minutes to three\004.","Blind Allies","Baynard Kendrick"},
["02:49"]={"At \0032:49 a.m.\004, the town clerk walked back to the microphone and tapped it once again. The momentary silence was broken only by a pencil falling off a table and rolling across the floor.","Mightier Than the Sword","Jeffrey Archer"},
["02:50"]={"When it was \0032:50\004 and the bank, too, had not been attacked, it was clear this was not the day of the big coup.","The Locked Room","Maj Sjöwall & Per Wahlöö"},
["02:52"]={"It was an impulse, born of aloneness. It was \003eight minutes to three in the morning\004, Sunday morning.","A Song in the Morning","Gerald Seymour"},
["02:53"]={"They reached the first roadblock on the outskirts of the town of Bulawayo, and Craig checked his wrist-watch. It was \003seven minutes to three\004 in the morning.","The Leopard Hunts in Darkness","Wilbur Smith"},
["02:54"]={"The times have changed and I can tell you exactly when they did — The times changed at exactly \003six minutes to three\004 last Friday morning.","GB84","David Peace"},
["02:55"]={"The dashboard clock showed \003five minutes to three\004, later than Theo had expected. The road, narrow and deserted, opened palely before them, then slid under the wheels like a strip of torn and soiled linen.","The Children of Men","P.D. James"},
["02:56"]={"It was \0032:56\004 when the shovel touched the coffin. We all heard the sound and looked at each other.","Extremely Loud and Incredibly Close","Jonathan Safran Foer"},
["02:57"]={"It was \00302:57\004 GMT. Yahaya slipped from his hiding place and cradled the syringe he had robbed from the ship’s hospital in his right hand.","Life Probe","Michael McCollum"},
["02:59"]={"He climbed off his bed at \0032:59 a.m.\004, fully rested, fully alert, walked over to the large trunk in the middle of the cabin and lifted its lid.","Be Careful What You Wish For","Jeffrey Archer"},
